<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_plate_deathknight_m_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Blood Death Knight</span></h2>Crafted items are, for the most part, no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Blacksmith, for example, you can still equip anything Blacksmiths craft. <br/>
<br/>A few of the crafted pieces will be part of your Best-in-Slot set before you step into raid.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94265/haunted-steel-treads">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Treads</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94266/haunted-steel-greathelm">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Greathelm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Greathelm</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94267/haunted-steel-warboots">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Warboots" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_deathknight_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Warboots</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94268/haunted-steel-headguard">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Headguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_plate_deathknight_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Headguard</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94592/lionheart-executioner-reborn">
<img alt="Lionheart Executioner, Reborn" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_2h_blacksmithing_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lionheart Executioner, Reborn</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94580/bloodmoon-reborn">
<img alt="Bloodmoon, Reborn" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_52.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodmoon, Reborn</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87406/gauntlets-of-battle-command">
<img alt="Gauntlets of Battle Command" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_plate_raiddeathknight_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of Battle Command</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87407/bloodforged-warfists">
<img alt="Bloodforged Warfists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodforged Warfists</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87405/unyielding-bloodplate">
<img alt="Unyielding Bloodplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unyielding Bloodplate</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_warrior_strengthofarms.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid  Protection Warrior Trinkets</span></h2>Your trinket usage will be dictated by what it is that you and your raid need. A stamina trinket like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95811/soul-barrier">
<img alt="Soul Barrier" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Barrier</span></a> will make you the least likely to die, especially in a 25-man raiding environment, while a trinket like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94508/brutal-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_strengthofarms.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> can offer a blend of defensive utility and offensive utility through the raw secondary stats and the Strength proc effect. Trinkets like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95799/gaze-of-the-twins">
<img alt="Gaze of the Twins" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_spectralsight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gaze of the Twins</span></a> have a more offensive tilt, but we scale well with both Strength and Crit, both defensively and offensively, making it a very attractive trinket. <br/>
<br/>Changing trinkets on an encounter-by-encounter basis is encouraged.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ins>Offensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94508/brutal-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_strengthofarms.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> - This trinket might as well be in both the offensive and defensive sections of this guide. It provides valuable stats while also having a proc that roughly lines up with our <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=1719/recklessness">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_criticalstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Recklessness</span></a> window.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95799/gaze-of-the-twins">
<img alt="Gaze of the Twins" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_spectralsight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gaze of the Twins</span></a> - Because of how highly we value crit (whether through Riposte or raw crit), this trinket becomes very attractive.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95757/primordius-talisman-of-rage">
<img alt="Primordius' Talisman of Rage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_rampage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Primordius' Talisman of Rage</span></a> - This trinket offers similar utility to the trinket above, but does it slightly worse.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=93256/skullrender-medallion">
<img alt="Skullrender Medallion" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skullrender Medallion</span></a> - This trinket requires Revered with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1375/dominance-offensive">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dominance Offensive</span></a>. It can also be upgraded twice, unlike a lot of the other options on this list.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77530/ghost-iron-dragonling">
<img alt="Ghost Iron Dragonling" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_head_dragon_bronze.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Iron Dragonling</span></a> - Can be socketed with any stat of your choosing through Tinker's Gear sockets like <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77544/flashing-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Flashing Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashing Tinker's Gear</span></a>. Shares Tinker's Gear slots with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> if you're an Engineer.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81138/carbonic-carbuncle">
<img alt="Carbonic Carbuncle" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Carbonic Carbuncle</span></a> - This trinket brings less defensive utility than the other options on this list, but has a very strong 30 sec proc which translates into a lot of damage during your opener with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=1719/recklessness">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_criticalstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Recklessness</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114207/skull-banner">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/warrior_skullbanner.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skull Banner</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=12292/bloodbath">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bloodbath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodbath</span></a>. Has a long ICD, so may not be worth using on some fights.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> - Offers <b>a lot</b> of avoidance through the Strength to Parry conversion and is your best offensive trinket in fights where you don't get super high Vengeance. It's a very expensive trinket to purchase, so don't feel bad about missing out on it, especially if you're raiding in a 25-player environment.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Defensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95811/soul-barrier">
<img alt="Soul Barrier" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Barrier</span></a> - This is by far your best defensive trinket in Phase 3 and is realistically the only fully defensive trinket worth considering.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=91210/tyrannical-gladiators-emblem-of-tenacity">
<img alt="Tyrannical Gladiator's Emblem of Tenacity" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_endlessrage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tyrannical Gladiator's Emblem of Tenacity</span></a> - The second-best defensive trinket in Phase 3 comes from PVP. This trinket can also be used effectively in fights where you get Vengeance cap in order to extend that cap with the on-use health effect. The trinket's on-use does not share cooldown with other trinkets or tinkers.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95727/ji-kuns-rising-winds">
<img alt="Ji-Kun's Rising Winds" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_heal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ji-Kun's Rising Winds</span></a> - This trinket is a bit of an outlier and provides a somewhat balanced profile. It has A LOT more value in 10-man than in 25-man.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a> - The 8871 Dodge also translates into solid offensive utility. This is a crafted BOE trinket, but it does not come with a very steep price tag.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89079/lao-chins-liquid-courage">
<img alt="Lao-Chin's Liquid Courage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lao-Chin's Liquid Courage</span></a> - This trinket has similar defensive utility to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a> but only offers defensive utility.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86881/stuff-of-nightmares">
<img alt="Stuff of Nightmares" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trinketpanda_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stuff of Nightmares</span></a> - This trinket offers less defensive utility than the Stamina counterparts, but does bring more offensive utility.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86790/vial-of-dragons-blood">
<img alt="Vial of Dragon's Blood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Dragon's Blood</span></a> - Similar to the above option, just worse.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Protection Warrior</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit and 15% Expertise. Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei racial Heroic Presence, will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your attacks will no longer miss Raid bosses. We prioritize Hit in our gearing, as even though it scales linearly to Expertise. Some abilities, like <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=6343/thunder-clap">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_thunderclap.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thunder Clap</span></a>, can miss but can't be dodged or parried.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>Expertise was changed to no longer grant reduction to <i>both</i> the target's ability to dodge <i>and</i> parry. When reaching 7.5% Expertise, you will have removed the boss's chance to dodge, but their chance to parry will remain unchanged. You'll need an additional 7.5% Expertise to eliminate their chance to parry (15% total). <br/>
<br/>This means that while tanking a target, there is effectively no "soft cap" where Expertise starts dropping off in value. However, as you're not always dealing damage to a target head-on, it's still worth thinking about Expertise in terms of a soft cap and hard cap. It's worth noting that if Shield Slam and Revenge is dodged or parried, they grant no Rage.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Protection Warrior</span></h2>Your gems will alternate depending on what you and your raid prioritize. We generally have 3 different playstyles (<i>Offensive</i>, <i>Balanced</i>, and <i>Defensive</i>), and below you'll find the appropriate gems for each playstyle. We generally opt to socket for the socket bonus, but if the bonus does not offer an attractive bonus, then opt for the<b> main gem</b> of each category. <br/>
<br/>
<b>
<span class="q5">Legendary Meta Gem:</span></b> In Phase 3 of Mists of Pandaria, we get access to two new meta gems that provide far greater utility than the normal meta gems. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95344/indomitable-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Indomitable Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Primal Diamond</span></a> and <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> are the two we can realistically use, and for most people, it should not be much of a choice. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95344/indomitable-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Indomitable Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Primal Diamond</span></a> provides the most utility overall with an outrageously high uptime, north of 50%. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> does scale with Vengeance and generally provides a 5-6% damage boost. <br/>
